{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22287 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Astersaponin F is implicated in the interaction with CX-1 through a series of target relationships, all mediated by dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. These kinases are targets of multiple compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, Javanicoside F, and Ascidiathiazone B, all of which are known to interact with Astersaponin F. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism by which Astersaponin F may influence cellular processes through these kinases, ultimately affecting CX-1. The evidence supports a pathway where Astersaponin F acts as a modulator of signaling pathways involving these kinases, which in turn may impact CX-1. The integration of these relationships highlights a possible role for Astersaponin F in regulating signaling cascades that involve multiple targets, with CX-1 being a downstream effector in this network.",
